     4	On v012 (arm 3), every empty patch is a timeout with zero edits, and no row lost its patch to a malformed `edit_file` or to running out of calls. Should I shelve the tool-level lever for the v012 lineage and let plan 010 (thinking 2048) address the time sink? Or do you still want a plan 011 arm?
     5	
     6	## 2. Pre-registration
     7	This is descriptive only, with no arm and no GPU. The question was written before tallying: do the arm-2 empty mechanisms (7 call-exhaustion never-edited, 3 malformed `edit_file`) recur on v012? Decision rule, fixed before tallying: if fewer than 3 of 33 v012 rows are non-timeout empties attributable to edit failure or call exhaustion, a tool-level lever has too few target rows to beat ±3 noise on 33. In that case I propose shelving it rather than spending an arm.
     8	
     9	## 3. What I did
    10	- Read the harness code. `edit_file`, `get_status` and the budget warning are fixed harness code that a bundle cannot change. The only budget signal is a `budget_warning` the harness attaches once 10 or fewer **calls** remain, at `swegemma/tools/base.py:47-63`. There is **no time warning**. The one tool path a bundle controls is a skill script: `run_skill_script` runs `python3` in the sandbox work dir (`adk_eval_core/sandbox/base.py:164+`), so a tolerant-edit helper is technically possible. Using it would still need prompt text, so the bundle would need its own score (dec 087).
    11	- Wrote `eval/plan011_empty_diag.py`, which tallies counts only and prints no task text. I ran it on the sealed arm-3 rows. No new runs.
    12	
    13	## 4. Results (arm 3 = 31b-v012-p9a, 33 dev ids, 1 sample per task)
    14	| class | main (31) | smoke (2) | total 33 |
    15	|---|---|---|---|
    16	| resolved | 10 | 0 | 10 |
    17	| empty, timeout, 0 edits | 16 | 2 | **18** |
    18	| empty, non-timeout (never edited or edit failed) | 0 | 0 | **0** |
    19	| patch, timeout | 2 | 0 | 2 |
    20	| patch, wrong | 3 | 0 | 3 |
    21	| malformed `edit_file` calls (rows) | 9 (1 row, resolved) | 0 | 9 (1) |
    22	
    23	Files: `results/plan011_diag_arm3_main.json`, `results/plan011_diag_arm3_smoke.json`. Classifier inputs: `results/plan009_arm3_{main,smoke}_d4cdf0f0.json`. The 18 empty-timeout rows used a median of 16.5 tool calls (range 5–41). In 5 of them the agent made 10 or fewer calls in the whole 210 s, so the clock ran out during model generation, not because calls ran out. That is the thinking-4096 time sink plan 010 targets. Script review: `codex-review` job `review-plan011-diag-light` (pending; numbers are provisional until it is CLEAN).
    24	
    25	## 5. Options
    26	- **A. Shelve the item-5 lever for the v012 lineage.** Re-check with the same script on plan-010 arm-4 rows: if non-timeout empties reach 3 or more there, bring a plan 011 then. Cost 0. Risk: none on current data.
    27	- **B. Build a plan 011 arm anyway:** a skill `safe_edit` helper plus prompt text telling the agent to edit by mid-budget. It has 0 target rows on v012 under the mechanism named in dec 081, and only the "edit earlier" part would touch the 18 timeouts. That part is prompt text, which dec 081 said this lever should not be. It would need its own score and would use about 9.7 h of Kaggle quota.
    28	- **C. Fold a time signal into plan 010's successor as a knob-only change,** e.g. analyzer thinking ≤2048. That stays finals-eligible under dec 087 (b). Decide after the arm-4 data.
    29	
    30	## 6. Recommendation
    31	A, with C kept as the follow-up after arm-4 data (week of 11-14). No requests: no SUBMIT, no GPU, no HOLDOUT.

